prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Read spam-classifier audit handoff\" $'**What**: Loaded the 2026-07-17 spam-classifier audit handoff: the strict random-letter regex yields 61 production candidates (26 not already spam), while the aggressive regex yields 388 unknowns and performs poorly on proxy datasets; no production code was changed.\\n**Why**: The user asked to continue from the handoff and the next step is external research before labeling candidates or changing production.\\n**Where**: handoff-2026-07-17-2042.md; src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/; scripts/ml/spam/.\\n**Learned**: Existing golden/field labels are Sonnet proxies, production differs from documented few-shot evaluation, and unrelated workspace changes must not be touched.' --type discovery --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Found unanswered conversations pass into downstream analysis\" $'**What**: Confirmed that conversations with zero customer messages are skipped only by SpamFilterStage, then pass into ClassifyStage because they are absent from spam_hashes; classify creates classification and entity LLM tasks for them.\\n**Why**: The user correctly challenged that no-customer-message records represent unanswered outbound attempts rather than useful customer conversations.\\n**Where**: src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/stage.py::_route_cascade, src/insights/pipeline/flows/_analyze_daily.py::_run_day_stages, src/insights/pipeline/stages/classify/stage.py::ClassifyStage.run.\\n**Learned**: Current design conflates not-spam with eligible-for-analysis. If unanswered attempts should not be analyzed, they need a separate eligibility gate/bucket rather than being labeled spam.' --type discovery --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["engram", "--help"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["engram", "session", "--help"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: spam regex audit and dead-branch removal\" $'## Goal\\nUnderstand the current spam-classifier design, research regex-based spam detection, and remove the unreachable no-customer-message branch.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Explain architecture with inline ASCII diagrams, not Mermaid.\\n- Keep explanations concise and junior-friendly.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- Production flow is won bypass → regex legit rescue → fused model thresholds → LLM gray zone.\\n- Random-letter regex remains shadow/audit-only.\\n- CrmFetcher enforces _INBOUND_MIN=1 non-empty inbound message for closed and active windows.\\n- Local dated corpus: 335,140 rows / 328,646 unique conversations / zero without customer messages.\\n- _index.jsonl intentionally omits messages and is not a daily SpamFilterStage input.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Researched SpamAssassin, Rspamd, Unicode, OWASP, and RE2; concluded regex should be a signal, not a destructive final verdict.\\n- Removed the actor_msgs-empty early continue from SpamFilterStage._route_cascade.\\n- Removed obsolete test_spam_filter_no_customer_messages_passes_through.\\n- Verified spam-filter and fetcher tests, ruff, source ty, targeted prek, and git diff check.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Continue evaluating the strict random-letter regex as a shadow candidate signal; do not deploy the aggressive variant.\\n- Review the 61 strict candidates before any production behavior change.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/stage.py — cascade orchestration; branch removed.\\n- tests/unit/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/test_spam_filter_stage.py — obsolete test removed.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/sources/db/fetcher.py — upstream inbound-text invariant.\\n- tests/unit/pipeline/sources/test_fetcher.py — invariant coverage.\\n- handoff-2026-07-17-2042.md — audit context.' --type session_summary --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: spam guard pushed\" $'## Goal\\nRemove and push the unreachable no-customer-message branch, then continue reviewing the current spam architecture visually.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Use inline ASCII diagrams, never Mermaid, for this architecture discussion.\\n- Keep explanations concise and junior-friendly.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- CrmFetcher enforces one non-empty inbound message before records reach SpamFilterStage.\\n- Unrelated voice-scoring working-tree files can break the full pre-push suite when hooks stash only tracked changes.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Removed the redundant no-customer guard and obsolete test.\\n- Committed c532cf73: refactor(spam): rely on inbound fetch invariant.\\n- Pushed to origin/feat/exit-sentiment-svm-cascade from a clean detached worktree.\\n- Full pre-push pytest, build, and dependency audit passed in the clean worktree.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Review the next node in the production diagram: regex rules that rescue obvious legitimate leads.\\n- Then review fused-model routing and LLM gray-zone behavior.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/stage.py — current cascade.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/rules.py — legitimate-rescue regex rules.\\n- tests/unit/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/test_spam_filter_stage.py — stage tests.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/sources/db/fetcher.py — inbound eligibility gate.' --type session_summary --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Persisted compacted spam-filter session context\" $'## Goal\\nMeasure and explain how effective the current reverse regex is at rescuing legitimate conversations in the spam cascade.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Respond concisely in Spanish for a junior SWE.\\n- Use inline ASCII diagrams, never Mermaid.\\n- Preserve unrelated working-tree changes.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- Current regex is a conservative legitimate-lead rescue, not a spam detector.\\n- Spam cascade is rescue rules -> fused model -> LLM.\\n- Upstream fetch requires at least one non-empty inbound customer message.\\n- Dated corpus has 335,140 rows, 328,646 unique conversations, and zero customerless conversations; Sonnet labels are proxies rather than human ground truth.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Removed the redundant no-customer-message guard and obsolete test.\\n- Targeted tests, Ruff, prek, and clean pre-push checks passed.\\n- Committed c532cf73 (refactor(spam): rely on inbound fetch invariant) and pushed origin/feat/exit-sentiment-svm-cascade.\\n- Started aggregate evaluation script /tmp/spam_rescue_eval.py in exec session 46180.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Poll session 46180, interpret rescue coverage and proxy false-rescue rates, save findings, and answer the user.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/rules.py — legitimate-lead rescue regexes.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/stage.py — spam cascade routing.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/sources/db/fetcher.py — inbound-message invariant.\\n- /tmp/spam_rescue_eval.py — uncommitted aggregate evaluation script.' --type session_summary --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Measured legitimate-rescue regex quality\" $'**What**: Evaluated the current reverse regex/rules on the production corpus and two Sonnet-proxy labeled sets. It rescues 15,567 of 259,582 eligible production conversations (5.997%). On golden labels, rescued items are 98.643% proxy-legitimate, legitimate recall is 10.476%, and 3/1,108 proxy-spam items are falsely rescued (0.271%). On field labels, rescued items are 98.724% proxy-legitimate, legitimate recall is 7.128%, and 5/108 proxy-spam items are falsely rescued (4.63%).\\n**Why**: The user asked how effective the current regex is at rescuing clearly legitimate leads before the model and LLM.\\n**Where**: src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/rules.py; scripts/ml/spam/data/spam_golden.jsonl; scripts/ml/spam/data/field_results.jsonl; dated conversation corpus; /tmp/spam_rescue_eval.py.\\n**Learned**: The rescue rules are precise but low-coverage: when they fire they are about 98.7% correct against proxy labels, but they rescue only 6% of eligible production traffic and 7-10% of proxy-legitimate cases. Field false-rescue rate is unstable because only 108 proxy-spam examples exist; all labels are Sonnet proxies, not human ground truth.' --type discovery --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Chose three-way spam model benchmark\" $'**What**: User chose to compare exactly three score models: TF-IDF + SVM, embeddings + XGBoost, and embeddings + logistic regression.\\n**Why**: They want to audit whether the current spam scoring model should be replaced.\\n**Where**: Experimental evaluation under scripts/ml/spam data; no production code change yet.\\n**Learned**: Keep representations separate for an interpretable comparison rather than using the current fused embedding+TF-IDF model.' --type decision --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Benchmarked three spam score models\" $'**What**: Compared TF-IDF + calibrated LinearSVC, 1024-d embeddings + XGBoost, and 1024-d embeddings + logistic regression using 5-fold StratifiedGroupKFold. Exact normalized duplicates stayed in one fold; a second stress test held out entire users/tenants. Exact-text F1/AP: SVM 0.7834/0.8775, XGBoost 0.8378/0.9305, LogReg 0.8143/0.9173. Unseen-tenant F1/AP: SVM 0.7347/0.8197, XGBoost 0.7924/0.8980, LogReg 0.7978/0.8854.\\n**Why**: User requested a direct three-way alternative-model audit.\\n**Where**: /tmp/compare_spam_models.py; scripts/ml/spam/data/spam_golden.jsonl; scripts/ml/spam/data/spam_emb.npz. No production files changed.\\n**Learned**: Embeddings clearly outperform TF-IDF for this proxy dataset. XGBoost ranks best overall, while LogReg is nearly tied on unseen tenants, trains much faster, and produces a smaller but safer high-confidence zone. The benchmark has only 3,189 Sonnet-proxy labels and cannot decide production behavior without an independent natural-distribution field set containing embeddings.' --type discovery --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: spam score model audit\" $'## Goal\\nAudit the shipped spam score model, quantify its data, and compare TF-IDF+SVM versus embeddings+XGBoost versus embeddings+logistic regression.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Explain concisely in Spanish for a junior SWE.\\n- Use inline ASCII diagrams, never Mermaid.\\n- Do not touch unrelated working-tree changes.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- Current production is fused embeddings+TF-IDF+XGBoost, not embedding-only XGBoost.\\n- It uses 3,189 Sonnet-proxy training rows: 1,108 spam and 2,081 legit; 2,964 unique normalized texts, 99 users, largest user 34%.\\n- Independent field labels contain 7,198 unique rows and 127 proxy spam but do not persist embeddings.\\n- Production XGBoost is uncalibrated despite docs claiming isotonic calibration; p>0.97 achieved only 93.33% proxy precision on reconstructed production-like field inputs.\\n- Three-way grouped benchmark: exact-text F1 SVM 0.7834, XGB 0.8378, LogReg 0.8143; unseen-tenant F1 SVM 0.7347, XGB 0.7924, LogReg 0.7978.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Mapped training/export/inference paths and artifact metadata.\\n- Measured dataset composition, duplicate/tenant concentration, calibration, field thresholds, and independent ranking metrics.\\n- Ran the requested 5-fold grouped benchmark in /tmp; Ruff passed.\\n- Consulted official scikit-learn calibration and sparse-text guidance.\\n- No production files changed.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Add current fused production model as an apples-to-apples reference if desired.\\n- Persist or regenerate embeddings for the 5,145 production-like field rows and compare the three candidates on natural prevalence.\\n- Human-label the destructive high-score zone before choosing p_spam or replacing production.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- /tmp/compare_spam_models.py — requested three-way benchmark.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/_assets/spam_model.joblib — shipped fused XGBoost.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/model.py — feature assembly and inference.\\n- scripts/ml/spam/data/spam_golden.jsonl — proxy training labels.\\n- scripts/ml/spam/data/spam_emb.npz — 1,024-dimensional embeddings.\\n- scripts/ml/spam/data/field_results.jsonl — independent proxy field scores.\\n- scripts/ml/spam/03_train.py — experimental training.\\n- scripts/ml/spam/06_export_prod.py — production export.\\n- docs/adr/0015-spam-cascade-thresholds-and-rollback.md — threshold safety contract.' --type session_summary --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/uv-cache uv run python /tmp/embed_spam_field.py"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Completed full spam score calibration audit\" $'**What**: Generated 1,024-d embeddings for all 5,145 production-like field rows (103 Sonnet-proxy spam) and evaluated TF-IDF+SVM, embeddings+XGBoost, embeddings+LogReg, plus shipped fused XGBoost. Cross-fitted sigmoid and isotonic calibrators by exact text and by user. Field AP/AUROC: SVM .53072/.95544; embedding XGB .66349/.96430; embedding LogReg .58553/.96678; current fused XGB .69366/.97020. Sigmoid won log loss/Brier for every model and generalized better by user than isotonic. Current fused sigmoid log loss .039397 and Brier .010121 were best.\\n**Why**: User requested measurement of ranking, calibration, thresholds, coverage, errors, confidence, cost, and slices—not just F1.\\n**Where**: /tmp/spam_field_embeddings.npz; /tmp/calibrate_spam_scores.py; /tmp/spam_score_calibration_results.json; existing golden/field datasets and production artifact. No production code changed.\\n**Learned**: Current fused model remains the best reference after proper natural-distribution evaluation. Its raw score is overconfident: a raw .97 maps to about .885 under the full-field sigmoid candidate; a calibrated .97 needs roughly raw .993. Cross-fitted calibrated .10/.97 routes 96.83% auto-legit, 2.92% LLM, .25% auto-spam, but misses 21/103 proxy spam on the auto-legit side. The 13 auto-spam examples were all proxy spam, yet their 95% Wilson precision lower bound is only 77.19%, so data is far too small to certify 99% precision. Human/future labels remain the blocker. Field embeddings used 766,271 tokens, 13.9 seconds, and estimated market cost US$0.01533.' --type discovery --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Designed TF-IDF SVM shadow sidecar\" $'**What**: The SVM shadow will load from a separate artifact, score only post-rescue candidates, and persist source hash, raw margin, calibrated proxy probability, model version, and the current pipeline\\'s final spam decision in a separate daily JSONL sidecar. It never changes routing.\\n**Why**: Per-row durable scores are needed to compare the candidate with current cascade/LLM decisions while keeping rollout safe and avoiding message text/PII in the artifact.\\n**Where**: src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/model.py, stage.py, schemas.py; scripts/train_spam_model.py; spam-filter tests; _assets/spam_svm_shadow.joblib.\\n**Learned**: Enable shadow by artifact presence to avoid changing the shared configuration surface; calibration is provisional sigmoid fitted from grouped out-of-fold proxy labels and must be replaced after human field labels.' --type architecture --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Trained TF-IDF SVM shadow artifact\" $'**What**: Trained the separate TF-IDF character+word+dense LinearSVC artifact with a sigmoid LogisticRegression calibrator on grouped out-of-fold margins. Artifact version is tfidf-svm-sigmoid-v1-958f24a7088c and size is 0.323 MB.\\n**Why**: The shadow integration needs a reproducible local scorer while current production routing remains unchanged.\\n**Where**: scripts/train_spam_model.py and src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/_assets/spam_svm_shadow.joblib.\\n**Learned**: Training used 3,189 Sonnet-proxy rows across 2,964 normalized-text groups; grouped CV AP=0.901635, AUROC=0.947372, Brier=0.087062, log loss=0.280397. These oversampled proxy metrics and probabilities are explicitly not production-approved.' --type discovery --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["git", "restore", "--source=HEAD"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Contained malformed shadow score failures\" $'**What**: Moved result-length validation and row assembly inside the shadow scorer\\'s failure boundary so exceptions or incomplete arrays return no shadow rows instead of aborting spam routing.\\n**Why**: Shadow deployment must be observational only; even a malformed candidate-model response cannot affect the production cascade or LLM.\\n**Where**: src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/stage.py and test_svm_shadow_failure_does_not_change_routing.\\n**Learned**: Catching only the model call was insufficient because strict zipping and aggregation could still raise afterward.' --type bugfix --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Separated SVM shadow trainer and nested calibration evaluation\" $'**What**: Preserved scripts/train_spam_model.py for the current production artifact and added scripts/train_spam_svm_shadow.py for the separate SVM candidate. Calibration metrics now use nested StratifiedGroupKFold, while the final sigmoid is fitted on grouped out-of-fold margins.\\n**Why**: Reusing the production trainer would break its existing operational contract, and non-nested calibration evaluation could leak validation-group information indirectly.\\n**Where**: scripts/train_spam_svm_shadow.py, src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/model.py, and spam_svm_shadow.joblib.\\n**Learned**: Nested grouped CV produced AP=0.901654, AUROC=0.947345, Brier=0.087149, and log loss=0.280610 on the oversampled Sonnet-proxy golden set; probabilities remain shadow-only.' --type decision --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Implemented TF-IDF SVM shadow scorer\" $'**What**: Added a versioned TF-IDF char+word+dense LinearSVC artifact with sigmoid calibration, a cached shadow loader, failure-isolated scoring after legitimate-rescue rules, and privacy-safe daily sidecar rows containing only source_hash, model version, margin, probability, and current final spam decision. Production routing is unchanged.\\n**Why**: User chose TF-IDF + SVM and wanted to validate it on real traffic before enabling auto-legit or auto-spam decisions.\\n**Where**: scripts/train_spam_svm_shadow.py; src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/{model.py,schemas.py,stage.py,_assets/spam_svm_shadow.joblib}; tests/unit/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/{test_spam_model.py,test_spam_cascade.py}.\\n**Learned**: Artifact presence enables shadow safely; it is 0.323 MB, version tfidf-svm-sigmoid-v1-958f24a7088c, and carries production_approved=false because calibration uses Sonnet-proxy labels. All 41 spam-filter tests and all prek hooks pass.' --type architecture --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: implemented TF-IDF SVM shadow\" $'## Goal\\nImplement the chosen TF-IDF + LinearSVC spam scorer in safe shadow mode without changing production routing.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Explain concisely in junior-friendly Spanish.\\n- Use ASCII diagrams, never Mermaid.\\n- Preserve unrelated working-tree changes.\\n- Use uv, Ruff, ty, pytest, and prek.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- A separate trainer is required so the existing production-model trainer contract is preserved.\\n- Sigmoid calibration evaluation needs nested grouped cross-validation to avoid indirect validation-group leakage.\\n- The final artifact is 0.323 MB, version tfidf-svm-sigmoid-v1-958f24a7088c, trained on 3,189 Sonnet-proxy rows across 2,964 normalized-text groups.\\n- Nested proxy CV: AP 0.901654, AUROC 0.947345, Brier 0.087149, log loss 0.280610; these are not natural-field or human metrics.\\n- Shadow row assembly must be inside the failure boundary; otherwise malformed result lengths could interrupt production routing.\\n- Full repository pytest is blocked by unrelated environment/worktree issues: Docker unavailable for pgvector tests, sandbox semaphore/physical-core failures, and an unrelated untracked 929-line voice_scoring router violating the god-file budget.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Added scripts/train_spam_svm_shadow.py with TF-IDF char+word+dense, LinearSVC, grouped out-of-fold sigmoid calibration, and nested grouped CV metrics.\\n- Generated spam_svm_shadow.joblib with production_approved=false metadata.\\n- Extended SpamModel to load and score the separate SVM artifact while preserving current fused behavior.\\n- Integrated post-rescue shadow scoring and a privacy-safe 01c_spam_svm_shadow.jsonl sidecar containing no message text.\\n- Current cascade/LLM remains the sole routing authority; shadow failures degrade to no shadow output.\\n- Added model, persistence, no-routing-change, and failure-isolation tests.\\n- 41 spam-filter tests pass; Ruff, targeted ty, and every prek hook pass.\\n- Preserved all unrelated working-tree changes; nothing was staged, committed, or pushed.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Run the pipeline on fresh or forced days to accumulate shadow sidecars. Cache-hit days do not rescore automatically.\\n- Join sidecar scores with human labels, especially short WhatsApp messages and boundary/high-margin cases.\\n- Refit the sigmoid on natural human-labeled field data and select the auto-legit threshold.\\n- Enable auto-legit gradually; keep auto-spam disabled until sufficient human evidence exists.\\n- Commit/push the implementation only when requested.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- scripts/train_spam_svm_shadow.py — reproducible SVM shadow trainer.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/_assets/spam_svm_shadow.joblib — versioned 0.323 MB artifact.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/model.py — artifact loading and margin/probability scoring.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/schemas.py — privacy-safe sidecar schema.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/stage.py — failure-isolated shadow integration and sidecar writing.\\n- tests/unit/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/test_spam_model.py — loader/artifact tests.\\n- tests/unit/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/test_spam_cascade.py — no-routing-change and failure tests.' --type session_summary --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "SKIP=pytest-backend git push"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Pushed TF-IDF SVM shadow scorer\" $'**What**: Committed and pushed the TF-IDF + LinearSVC shadow implementation as 4574ec48 (feat(spam): add TF-IDF SVM shadow scorer) to origin/feat/exit-sentiment-svm-cascade.\\n**Why**: User explicitly requested pushing the completed shadow scorer.\\n**Where**: Seven spam-specific files: trainer, joblib artifact, model/schema/stage integration, and two test files.\\n**Learned**: The pre-push pytest-backend hook was skipped only after it failed for unrelated Docker-unavailable job-queue tests, unrelated voice-scoring/sentiment failures, and coverage. The spam suite (41 tests), lint, typecheck, build, audit, and other hooks passed. Hook-created sentiment joblib changes were reverted; all unrelated working-tree changes remain unstaged.' --type config --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: pushed TF-IDF SVM shadow\" $'## Goal\\nCommit and push the completed TF-IDF + LinearSVC spam shadow scorer.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Push only spam-shadow changes.\\n- Preserve all unrelated working-tree changes.\\n- No generated attribution or co-author lines.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- The pre-push pytest-backend hook cannot pass locally because Docker is unavailable for pgvector/job-queue tests; unrelated untracked voice-scoring and sentiment work also causes failures and lowers coverage to 83%.\\n- The failed hook modified two sentiment joblib files; those hook-created changes were reverted to HEAD without touching preexisting sentiment source changes.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Staged exactly seven spam-shadow files.\\n- Created commit 4574ec48: feat(spam): add TF-IDF SVM shadow scorer.\\n- Commit hooks passed.\\n- Pushed to origin/feat/exit-sentiment-svm-cascade.\\n- Skipped only pytest-backend during the successful push; uv build, pip-audit, formatting, large-file checks, 41 spam tests, Ruff, ty, and prek passed.\\n- Verified local branch and remote both point to 4574ec48.\\n- Preserved all unrelated working-tree changes unstaged.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Run fresh or forced pipeline days to collect 01c_spam_svm_shadow.jsonl data.\\n- Human-label disagreements and recalibrate before enabling auto-legit.\\n- Keep auto-spam disabled until sufficient reviewed evidence exists.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- scripts/train_spam_svm_shadow.py — reproducible trainer.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/_assets/spam_svm_shadow.joblib — shadow artifact.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/model.py — loader/scorer.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/schemas.py — sidecar schema.\\n- src/insights/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/stage.py — shadow integration.\\n- tests/unit/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/test_spam_model.py — model tests.\\n- tests/unit/pipeline/stages/spam_filter/test_spam_cascade.py — routing isolation tests.' --type session_summary --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["engram", "context"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["engram", "timeline"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Created comprehensive spam session summary\" $'**What**: Added a root Markdown document consolidating the complete spam-detection audit, benchmark, calibration results, shadow implementation, conclusions, and next steps.\\n**Why**: The user requested one durable summary of everything completed in the session.\\n**Where**: spam-session-summary-2026-07-18.md\\n**Learned**: The summary must clearly separate proxy cross-validation from natural-field evaluation and distinguish current production routing from the non-routing TF-IDF + SVM shadow.' --type discovery --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Closed spam audit documentation session\" $'## Goal\\nCreate a root Markdown file summarizing the complete spam-detection session, including work performed, conclusions, measurements, implementation, and next steps.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Write in concise Spanish for a junior software engineer.\\n- Use ASCII diagrams, never Mermaid.\\n- Preserve all unrelated workspace changes.\\n- Do not commit or push unless explicitly requested.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- The durable summary must distinguish the current production XGBoost route from the TF-IDF + SVM shadow, which does not affect routing.\\n- Proxy cross-validation results are not directly comparable to evaluation on the natural field dataset.\\n- The first verification attempt failed because uv could not write to its default cache; UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/uv-cache resolved it.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Created a 733-line comprehensive session summary with the architecture, datasets, regex/rescue rules, benchmark results, calibration, thresholds, slice analysis, runtime/cost, shadow implementation, commits, conclusions, and recommended next steps.\\n- Verified all required sections are present and that the document contains no Mermaid diagram.\\n- Left the document untracked; no commit or push was performed in this documentation task.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Review the document with the user.\\n- Commit and push it only if the user explicitly requests that.\\n- Continue collecting real shadow data and build a human-labeled validation set before changing production routing.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- spam-session-summary-2026-07-18.md — Complete session summary created at the repository root.' --type discovery --project vambe-datascience --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Seek approachable AI NLP ML open-source repositories\" $'**What**: User wants to contribute to active open-source repositories related to AI, NLP, and ML that are not overcrowded and accept outside contributions.\\n**Why**: They want a realistic path to becoming an open-source contributor.\\n**Where**: Future repository recommendations and contribution planning.\\n**Learned**: Prefer modest-size projects with clear contribution guidance and actionable beginner-friendly issues.' --type preference --project personal --scope personal"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Recommended GPJax issue 675 for first ML contribution\" $'**What**: Recommended GPJax issue #675 as the best first open-source code contribution, with small-text #48/#59, EuroEval #1663, and Pipelex #522 as alternatives.\\n**Why**: GPJax #675 is recent, unassigned, has no linked PR or comments, is labeled good first issue, uses Python and uv, and is directly reproducible on the user’s macOS machine.\\n**Where**: Repository selection for AI/NLP/ML open-source contribution work.\\n**Learned**: As of 2026-07-23, avoid skore good-first issues because both are already claimed; QWED issue #17 is stale because CONTRIBUTING.md already exists; quantulum3 and semantic-split beginner issues are years old.' --type decision --project personal --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: approachable AI NLP ML open-source search\" $'## Goal\\nFind active AI, NLP, and ML repositories that are not overcrowded and accept outside contributors.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Prefer Python projects with modest star/contributor counts, clear contribution guidance, and unclaimed beginner issues.\\n- Explain options and tradeoffs for a junior software engineer.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- GPJax #675 is recent, unassigned, has no comments or linked PR, uses uv, and is reproducible on macOS.\\n- small-text actively welcomes contributions and has unclaimed NLP issues #48 and #59.\\n- EuroEval is highly active, has 192 stars, and issue #1663 has no comments.\\n- Pipelex is active and welcoming; #522 is unclaimed but its scope should be clarified before coding.\\n- skore beginner issues are already claimed; QWED #17 is obsolete; quantulum3 and semantic-split beginner issues are stale.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Screened repositories by current activity, size, contribution guide, open good-first issues, comments, assignments, and linked PRs.\\n- Recommended GPJax #675 as the best first code contribution.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- User chooses a repository/issue.\\n- Before implementation, comment on the issue to claim/confirm scope, then fork, reproduce, patch, test, and open a PR.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- No local files changed.' --type session_summary --project personal --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Chose small-text for first NLP open-source contribution\" $'**What**: User chose webis-de/small-text and wants to evaluate possible features, prioritize efficient work, and contribute.\\n**Why**: small-text aligns better with the user’s goal of learning and contributing to NLP and machine learning rather than only LLM orchestration.\\n**Where**: Upcoming repository exploration, issue selection, implementation, and pull request work for webis-de/small-text.\\n**Learned**: Optimize for high-value, bounded changes with a strong chance of maintainer acceptance.' --type decision --project personal --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Ignored Serena project metadata in small-text\" $'**What**: Added `.serena/` to small-text’s `.gitignore`.\\n**Why**: Repository instructions require local Serena indexing metadata to stay out of Git.\\n**Where**: /Users/sebabreguel/personal/small-text/.gitignore' --type config --project small-text --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Require evidence-backed small-text contributions\" $'**What**: User authorized continuing autonomously on small-text and requires proposed features to be clear and supported by benchmarks against state-of-the-art methods or comparable libraries.\\n**Why**: Contributions should demonstrate measurable value rather than adding speculative functionality.\\n**Where**: Feature discovery, experimental design, implementation, and pull request justification for webis-de/small-text.\\n**Learned**: Prefer bounded features with reproducible baselines, explicit metrics, and comparisons to current literature or maintained libraries.' --type preference --project small-text --scope personal"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Built small-text code review graph\" $'**What**: Built the full code-review graph for small-text: 241 files, 2,430 nodes, 20,879 edges, 135 flows, and 18 communities.\\n**Why**: Needed architecture and impact analysis before selecting or implementing non-trivial contributions.\\n**Where**: Local code-review-graph index for /Users/sebabreguel/personal/small-text.\\n**Learned**: The graph built cleanly with no parser errors.' --type config --project small-text --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: small-text benchmark-backed contribution setup\" $'## Goal\\nEvaluate webis-de/small-text for an efficient open-source NLP/ML contribution, identify clear feature opportunities, and support them with reproducible benchmarks against current research or maintained libraries.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Explain decisions concisely in Spanish for a junior software engineer.\\n- Research before non-trivial code and compare tradeoffs.\\n- Prefer bounded, maintainer-friendly contributions with evidence.\\n- Benchmark candidates against state-of-the-art methods or maintained libraries.\\n- Use uv, ruff, ty, pytest, and prek for Python verification.\\n- Follow repository navigation rules: graph for architecture/impact and Serena for symbols/edits.\\n- Do not commit plan documents, generated attribution, or secrets.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- small-text is an active-learning library for text classification with scikit-learn, PyTorch, Transformers, and optional Argilla integrations.\\n- Existing issue #48 requests consistent float32 embeddings across EmbeddingMixin implementations and appears suitable as a small trust-building fix.\\n- Existing issue #59 is README-only; #14 concerns multilabel probability behavior and is more involved.\\n- Potential modern query-strategy gaps must still be verified against the current code and primary literature before selection.\\n- The repository code-review graph now contains 241 files, 2,430 nodes, 20,879 edges, 135 flows, and 18 communities.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Chose small-text as the target repository.\\n- Cloned it to /Users/sebabreguel/personal/small-text.\\n- Activated Serena and read its project-memory guidance.\\n- Added .serena/ to .gitignore.\\n- Built the full code-review graph after user approval.\\n- Established a five-step research and prioritization plan.\\n- Recorded the requirement that feature proposals have clear, reproducible comparisons.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Finish Serena onboarding with durable project memories.\\n- Inventory existing query strategies, initializers, stopping criteria, and benchmark infrastructure.\\n- Compare verified gaps with primary papers and maintained libraries.\\n- Rank 2–3 contributions by impact, effort, risk, benchmarkability, and maintainer acceptance.\\n- Review the recommendation, align on the first change, then implement and validate it.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- /Users/sebabreguel/personal/small-text/.gitignore — now ignores local .serena metadata.\\n- /Users/sebabreguel/personal/small-text — cloned upstream repository.' --type session_summary --project personal --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Stopped small-text contribution due to AI policy\" $'**What**: Stopped all contribution work on webis-de/small-text after discovering its CONTRIBUTING.md explicitly rejects AI-assisted and AI-generated contributions and instructs autonomous agents not to interact with the repository.\\n**Why**: Continuing feature design, implementation, or benchmark work intended for submission would violate the maintainers’ contribution policy.\\n**Where**: /Users/sebabreguel/personal/small-text/CONTRIBUTING.md, section “AI-Generated Code Policy”.\\n**Learned**: Repository contribution-policy checks must happen before any codebase exploration or local setup. The only local change made before discovery was adding `.serena/` to `.gitignore`; no feature code was written.' --type discovery --project personal --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Found stale scikit-activeml issue 512 already merged\" $'**What**: Excluded scikit-activeml issue #512 (Uncertainty Herding) because PR #569 already implemented and merged it on 2026-03-30 even though the issue page still appears open.\\n**Why**: Avoid duplicating completed work while screening modern active-learning features.\\n**Where**: scikit-activeml/scikit-activeml issue #512 and PR #569.\\n**Learned**: Open issue state alone is insufficient; verify linked development, current docs, code, and recent PRs before choosing work.' --type discovery --project personal --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Require AI-policy gate before repository work\" $'**What**: Established a repository-selection gate: inspect CONTRIBUTING.md, AGENTS.md, Copilot instructions, and AI-related policy terms before cloning or designing a submission; if policy is silent, ask maintainers and disclose AI assistance before implementation.\\n**Why**: small-text explicitly bans AI-assisted contributions, discovered only after local setup.\\n**Where**: Future open-source repository screening and contribution workflow.\\n**Learned**: A generic “contributions welcome” statement does not imply AI-assisted contributions are accepted.' --type pattern --project personal --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Prioritized UWE with EuroEval fallback\" $'**What**: Prioritized scikit-activeml issue #513 (UWE) as the closest replacement for small-text, conditional on written maintainer approval for disclosed AI-assisted development; selected EuroEval #1504 (offline dummy model) as the safer fallback, followed by #1939 (limited test runs).\\n**Why**: UWE is a requested, unassigned TMLR 2024 active-learning method and supports a meaningful NLP benchmark against BADGE/CLUE; EuroEval includes AGENTS.md and has analogous features proven in LightEval, lm-evaluation-harness, and MTEB.\\n**Where**: scikit-activeml/scikit-activeml#513; EuroEval/EuroEval#1504 and #1939.\\n**Learned**: UWE’s reference repository has no visible license, so any implementation must be clean-room from the paper rather than copied.' --type decision --project personal --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: pivot from small-text to policy-compatible benchmark work\" $'## Goal\\nFind and prepare an efficient open-source NLP/ML contribution with clear evidence and reproducible benchmarks.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Explain decisions concisely in Spanish for a junior software engineer.\\n- Compare candidate features against primary papers or maintained libraries.\\n- Verify repository AI-contribution policy before cloning or implementation.\\n- Use bounded scope, tests, lint, type checks, and reproducible benchmarks.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- small-text explicitly prohibits AI-assisted and AI-generated contributions; all work there stopped immediately.\\n- scikit-activeml issue #512 looked open but Uncertainty Herding was already merged in PR #569 on 2026-03-30.\\n- scikit-activeml #513 requests UWE, a TMLR 2024 method generalizing BADGE; it has no assignee, comments, or linked PR. The repository policy is silent on AI assistance, so written approval is required first.\\n- The official UWE reference repository has no visible license; implementation must be clean-room from the paper.\\n- EuroEval contains AGENTS.md and no AI ban was found in CONTRIBUTING.md. Issue #1504 requests an offline dummy model, a pattern already used by LightEval, lm-evaluation-harness, and MTEB. Issue #1939 requests limited test runs, matching lm-eval --limit and LightEval max_samples.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Built and inspected the small-text graph before discovering the policy, then stopped without writing feature code.\\n- Screened Baal, scikit-activeml, EuroEval, AISteer360, ALToolbox, and related libraries.\\n- Verified current issues, comments, linked PRs, contribution rules, paper status, and competing-library precedents.\\n- Prioritized scikit-activeml #513 with a benchmark on intent classification; selected EuroEval #1504 and #1939 as safer fallbacks.\\n- Drafted a policy-safe next step: disclose AI assistance and request maintainer approval before touching scikit-activeml.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Get user approval to post the disclosure/ownership comment on scikit-activeml #513.\\n- If maintainers approve, clone, activate Serena, check/build graph, and inspect UWE/BADGE/CLUE extension points.\\n- Implement UWE independently from the paper with unit tests and documentation.\\n- Benchmark Random, Entropy, BADGE, CLUE, and UWE on Banking77/CLINC150 embeddings across multiple seeds, measuring learning-curve area, macro-F1/accuracy, query latency, and peak memory.\\n- If approval is denied or absent, pivot to EuroEval #1504.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- /Users/sebabreguel/personal/small-text/CONTRIBUTING.md — contains the blocking AI policy; do not continue contribution work.\\n- /Users/sebabreguel/personal/small-text/.gitignore — only local modification, adding .serena/ before policy discovery.' --type session_summary --project personal --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Ignored Serena metadata in vambeai-backend\" $'**What**: Added `.serena/` to `.gitignore`.\\n**Why**: Repository instructions require local Serena indexing metadata to stay out of Git.\\n**Where**: /Users/sebabreguel/vambe/voiceScoring/vambeai-backend/.gitignore' --type config --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Review PR fully before making edits\" $'**What**: User requested a complete review and simplification analysis of PR #12574 without applying inline/code changes yet.\\n**Why**: They want findings first and implementation only after explicit approval.\\n**Where**: vambeai-backend PR #12574 review workflow.' --type preference --project vambeai-backend --scope personal"], decision="allow")
