prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: vambeai-backend PR 12574 review\" $'## Goal\\nRevisar completamente PR #12574 con ce-code-review y simplification, sin editar código ni publicar comentarios.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Solo revisión completa; no cambios inline hasta aprobación explícita.\\n- Responder conciso en español y explicar términos para junior SWE.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- PR 20 archivos, +2152/-506; CI verde.\\n- Bloqueadores confirmados: telemetría registra contexto crudo de llamadas; deadline parcial sin cancelación; retry/fallback multiplicado; fanout sin límite/deduplicación; fallback de timeout pierde added_criteria.\\n- Hallazgos P2: contrato planner/create incompatible; requirements pueden perderse al filtrar keys inválidas; tests tienen diagnósticos TypeScript y mocks que omiten validación Zod.\\n- La supuesta incompatibilidad de rollout con frontend dev es falso positivo; frontend dev no contiene rutas ai-rubric. Desplegar backend antes que frontend.\\n- Migración JSONB metadata es aditiva y coherente, pero título/body del PR están desactualizados.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Revisión read-only completa y simplification analysis.\\n- Tests focalizados: 3 suites, 53 tests pasan.\\n- ESLint focalizado pasa.\\n- Final tech-lead verdict: Request changes.\\n- No se hicieron cambios tracked ni comentarios en GitHub.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Entregar reporte final ahora.\\n- Esperar autorización antes de implementar fixes o comentar el PR.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric-generation.service.ts — planner, judge, retries, deadline y fallbacks.\\n- src/openai/services/open-ai.service.ts — fallback de modelos y telemetría.\\n- src/voice-call-transcript/services/voice-call-transcript.service.ts — muestras crudas de llamadas.\\n- src/ai-rubric/schemas/ai-rubric-plan.schema.ts — límites del output.\\n- src/ai-rubric/dtos/create-ai-rubric.dto.ts — contrato de persistencia.\\n- src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric.service.spec.ts — diagnostics TypeScript y mock de save.\\n- src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric-generation.service.spec.ts — mock que evita parseo Zod.\\n- src/migrations/1784912437067-add-ai-rubric-call-type.ts — migración metadata JSONB.' --type session_summary --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Keep AI rubric planning guarantees in backend\" $'**What**: User decided validation, normalization, fallback completeness, time budgeting, and plan-to-create compatibility should be enforced by the backend rather than delegated to the frontend.\\n**Why**: The backend owns the AI pipeline and should return a complete persistable result to every caller.\\n**Where**: src/ai-rubric planner, schemas, DTOs, and tests for PR #12574.\\n**Learned**: Prefer backend normalization and a final persistable-output contract; frontend should render/save the returned plan without repairing it.' --type architecture --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Fixed PR 12574 AI rubric planner review findings\" $'**What**: Implemented the approved backend fixes for PR #12574: one 150s deadline across the whole pipeline with AbortSignal cancellation, one model-fallback retry dimension (`maxRetries: 0` inside each provider), deterministic fallbacks that retain `added_criteria`, backend plan normalization for invalid/duplicate keys and six-rubric cap, persistable 2,000-character descriptions, unique template input validation, and schema-aware/realistic tests. Telemetry behavior was intentionally left unchanged.\\n**Why**: User accepted private telemetry but requested fixes for timeouts, retry amplification, dropped requirements, planner/create contract drift, and misleading tests; all guarantees should live in backend.\\n**Where**: src/ai-rubric/{consts,dto,schemas,services}/, src/openai/service/openai.service.ts, and their specs.\\n**Learned**: AI SDK 6 `generateObject` supports `abortSignal`, and `maxRetries: 0` lets the shared model fallback loop be the only retry dimension. Rubric call context already uses stored transcript summaries; a second summarizer for generated descriptions would add cost and semantic drift, so schema enforcement plus source fallback is safer. The five-template catalog is still supplied in the request by frontend; only planning/normalization guarantees are now backend-owned.' --type bugfix --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: PR 12574 planner fixes\" $'## Goal\\nRevisar PR #12574, acordar los hallazgos con el usuario y aplicar los fixes aprobados sin push ni comentarios en GitHub.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Telemetría privada se acepta y no debe cambiarse.\\n- Deadline, retries, normalización, fallback y compatibilidad plan/create deben vivir en backend.\\n- No push/commit/comentarios sin aprobación.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- Hay cinco templates hoy y máximo un gap rubric; el riesgo real era duplicar/alucinar keys y el futuro contrato acepta hasta diez templates. Backend ahora deduplica y limita a seis rúbricas totales.\\n- Una key válida es exactamente una `template.key` enviada en `available templates`; una key inventada antes perdía `covers`.\\n- Los contextos de llamadas ya usan `transcript.summary` además de excerpts. No conviene otro summarizer para descripciones: schema máximo 2.000 + fallback al source evita costo y distorsión.\\n- AI SDK 6 soporta `abortSignal`; `maxRetries: 0` permite usar solo el fallback de modelos compartido.\\n- El catálogo de cinco templates todavía llega desde frontend en el request; mover el catálogo al backend sería otro cambio arquitectónico.\\n- El typecheck completo local queda bloqueado por errores ajenos al diff: dependencia `facturapi` ausente y propiedad `tier` inválida en llama-parse.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Deadline global de 150s desde entrada y cancelación de llamadas LLM.\\n- Eliminado retry externo duplicado; cada modelo se intenta una vez dentro del fallback compartido.\\n- Fallback y composición conservan `added_criteria`.\\n- Normalización backend de keys inválidas/duplicadas, cobertura, títulos y límite total.\\n- Descripciones AI alineadas con el contrato persistible de 2.000 caracteres.\\n- Fixtures TypeScript, orden realista de save y mocks Zod corregidos.\\n- 73 tests pasan; ESLint focalizado, knip y git diff --check pasan.\\n- No commit, push ni comentarios GitHub.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Usuario revisa el resumen/diff y decide si desea commit/push.\\n- Aclarar si “todo backend” también significa mover el catálogo de templates fuera del frontend; no se hizo aún.\\n- El typecheck global requiere arreglar/restaurar dependencias baseline ajenas a este cambio.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric-generation.service.ts — deadline, cancelación, normalización, retry policy y fallbacks.\\n- src/openai/service/openai.service.ts — executionOptions con abortSignal/maxRetries.\\n- src/ai-rubric/schemas/ai-rubric-plan.schema.ts — límite persistible compartido.\\n- src/ai-rubric/dto/ai-rubric-request.dto.ts — validación backend de templates/descripciones.\\n- src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric-generation.service.spec.ts — cobertura del pipeline y mocks schema-aware.\\n- src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric.service.spec.ts — fixture tipado y orden save realista.\\n- src/openai/service/openai.service.spec.ts — cancelación corta el fallback.' --type session_summary --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: PR 12574 push pending\" $'## Goal\\nRevisar PR #12574, aplicar los fixes aprobados y pushearlos.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Mantener telemetría privada sin cambios.\\n- Garantías del pipeline AI rubric deben vivir en backend.\\n- No incluir metadata/herramientas locales ni planes en el commit.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- El pipeline necesitaba deadline global con cancelación real, una sola dimensión de retry, normalización backend y fallback compatible con create.\\n- El typecheck global mantiene errores baseline ajenos en Facturapi y Llama Parse; los archivos tocados no agregan errores.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Implementados deadline global de 150s, AbortSignal, maxRetries=0 por proveedor, normalización de keys/covers/títulos/límite, fallback con added_criteria y límite compartido de descripción.\\n- Tests focalizados: 4 suites y 73 tests OK. ESLint focalizado, knip y diff --check OK.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Stagear solo los ocho archivos fuente/test, commitear y pushear la rama feat/ai-rubric-suggest-refine-sonnet al PR #12574.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- src/ai-rubric/consts/ai-rubric.consts.ts — límites compartidos.\\n- src/ai-rubric/dto/ai-rubric-request.dto.ts — contrato de request.\\n- src/ai-rubric/schemas/ai-rubric-plan.schema.ts — schema del plan.\\n- src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric-generation.service.ts — deadline, normalización y fallbacks.\\n- src/openai/service/openai.service.ts — structured completion cancelable.' --type session_summary --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["git", "diff", "--cached", "--check"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Pushed PR 12574 AI rubric hardening\" $'**What**: Committed and pushed the approved AI Rubric planner fixes to PR #12574 at commit 2f7f17a3695dab1d1dd2d4ef38c4aca3818d9c52.\\n**Why**: Resolve the agreed review findings around global deadlines, cancellation, retries, backend normalization, fallback completeness, and request limits.\\n**Where**: Branch feat/ai-rubric-suggest-refine-sonnet; https://github.com/vambeai/vambeai-backend/pull/12574\\n**Learned**: Only the eight reviewed source/test files were committed; local .context/, .serena/, data/, and plan-runs/ remain untracked.' --type bugfix --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Scoped voice-scoring document attachments to frontend-only phase 1\" $'**What**: Phase 1 only adds document attachment behavior in the rubric planner frontend section 2; OCR and rubric-planning integration remain out of scope until explicitly approved.\\n**Why**: The user narrowed the first step to attaching documents in the UI. Implementing OCR or planner changes now would exceed scope.\\n**Where**: Frontend branch feat/ai-rubric-window, mainly apps/mercur/src/components/voice-scoring/plan-rubrics-sections.tsx and plan-rubrics-dialog.tsx.\\n**Learned**: The remaining UX decision is local-only selection versus immediate upload to S3; no implementation should begin before that behavior is clarified and approved.' --type decision --project vambeai-backend --scope project --topic architecture/voice-scoring-document-attachments"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: read voice-scoring attachment handoff\" $'## Goal\\nRead and internalize /tmp/handoff-2026-07-29-1653.md for the voice-scoring document attachment task.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Phase 1 is frontend-only document attachment.\\n- Do not add OCR or rubric-planning integration without explicit scope expansion.\\n- Clarify UX one question at a time before implementation.\\n- Keep plans/design docs local and untracked.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- No code has been changed yet.\\n- The unresolved behavior is local-only file selection versus immediate S3 upload through the existing uploadFile helper.\\n- The frontend work belongs on feat/ai-rubric-window in the sibling vambe-turborepo-frontend repository.\\n- Backend Mistral OCR exists but is not wired to rubric uploads and is out of phase-1 scope.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Read the complete 228-line handoff and persisted its scope decision.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Ask whether the user wants a visual proposal or text-only discussion.\\n- Then clarify local selection versus immediate S3 upload before proposing and approving a design.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- /tmp/handoff-2026-07-29-1653.md — source handoff.\\n- ../vambe-turborepo-frontend/apps/mercur/src/components/voice-scoring/plan-rubrics-sections.tsx — target UI section.\\n- ../vambe-turborepo-frontend/apps/mercur/src/components/voice-scoring/plan-rubrics-dialog.tsx — dialog state/orchestration.\\n- ../vambe-turborepo-frontend/packages/api/src/assistants/infrastructure/upload-file.ts — existing presigned-S3 upload helper.' --type session_summary --project vambeai-backend --scope project --topic session/voice-scoring-attachments-handoff"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Limit rubric OCR attachments to two documents\" $'**What**: Agreed to allow a maximum of two documents per rubric planning request.\\n**Why**: Keep OCR and LLM processing bounded and the first version simple.\\n**Where**: Frontend document picker plus backend OCR/planning validation.\\n**Learned**: The frontend should prevent selecting more than two, but the backend must also reject requests above two because client limits are not security guarantees.' --type decision --project vambeai-backend --scope project --topic architecture/voice-scoring-document-attachments"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Ignored Serena metadata in toreto vambeai-backend\" $'**What**: Added `.serena/` to `.gitignore`.\\n**Why**: Repository instructions require local Serena indexing metadata to stay out of Git.\\n**Where**: /Users/sebabreguel/vambe/toreto/vambeai-backend/.gitignore' --type config --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
