prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Review PR-7143 fixes interactively one by one\" $'**What**: For every PR #7143 finding, present options and tradeoffs, get the user’s opinion, then implement that single fix before continuing.\\n**Why**: The user wants their opinion included in all fixes.\\n**Where**: PR-7143-REVIEW-VERDICT.md remediation workflow.\\n**Learned**: Tests and linters must not be run during this work.' --type preference --project toreto --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Warn before discarding unfinished PR-7143 rubric plan\" $'**What**: Use hybrid close behavior: after successful creation, “Listo” discards the completed plan silently; before completion, attempting to close must warn that the generated plan will be lost and only discard after explicit confirmation; during creation, closing remains blocked.\\n**Why**: The user does not want accidental plan loss and corrected the initial option A behavior.\\n**Where**: apps/mercur/src/components/voice-scoring/plan-rubrics-dialog.tsx.' --type decision --project toreto --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Reviewed PR 13331 rubric anchors\" $'**What**: Static review found five P2 blockers: Patience depends on prosody unavailable to transcript scoring; Support score 2 claims a failed re-question absent from its body; Quotes Retoma score 4 already satisfies product+date and only asks delivery channel; Empathy defaults to null on doubt while scoring PR #13276 assumes trigger on doubt; Support score 1 contains a partial cadence despite #13276 requiring minimum 2 for any partial attempt. Existing patience-null and sales-null comments are wording inconsistencies but non-blocking because rationales/global scorer define triggers.\\n**Why**: User requested a full read-only review of PR #13331 including existing comments.\\n**Where**: PR #13331; human-touch.template.ts, support.template.ts, quotes.template.ts; downstream ai-rubric-score.prompt.ts in PR #13276.\\n**Learned**: Anchor bodies, rationales, and scorer-wide null/minimum-score policies must agree because the pipeline is transcript-only and the rationale is the measuring rule.' --type discovery --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Keep rubric detail Sheet mounted through close animation\" $'**What**: Control the detail Sheet with an explicit open prop and retain the last selected rubric in RubricsView until Radix finishes its slide-out animation.\\n**Why**: The user chose the proper exit animation instead of removing or ignoring it.\\n**Where**: apps/mercur/src/components/voice-scoring/rubrics-view.tsx and rubric-detail-dialog.tsx.' --type decision --project vambe-turborepo-frontend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: audited all rubric templates\" $'## Goal\\nReview every Vambe phone rubric template for semantic coherence.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- Overall coverage, structure, and 100-point weights are coherent.\\n- Highest-risk issues are description/anchor contradictions and null applicability.\\n- Appointment date/time anchors omit required customer acceptance; alternatives score 3 claims evidence absent from its body.\\n- Quote capture anchors omit required recap/validation.\\n- Support empathy mixes universal respect with trigger-based null; verification anchors contradict requirements and scores 1/2 overlap.\\n- Human-touch respect relies partly on transcript-ambiguous tone.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Read and assessed all five templates: appointments, human-touch, quotes, sales, and support.\\n- Added a local .gitignore entry for Serena metadata.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- If requested, rank and patch the high-confidence semantic mismatches without broad refactoring.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- src/ai-rubric/rubric-templates/vambe-phone/appointments.template.ts — appointment rubric\\n- src/ai-rubric/rubric-templates/vambe-phone/human-touch.template.ts — communication rubric\\n- src/ai-rubric/rubric-templates/vambe-phone/quotes.template.ts — quote rubric\\n- src/ai-rubric/rubric-templates/vambe-phone/sales.template.ts — sales rubric\\n- src/ai-rubric/rubric-templates/vambe-phone/support.template.ts — support rubric\\n- src/ai-rubric/rubric-templates/.gitignore — ignores .serena/' --type session_summary --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Validated Codex retry and evidence findings in PR 13276\" $'**What**: At HEAD 8c2fe2a, criterion checkpoint invalidation is fixed with an id+updated_at key, while evidence quotes are still accepted and persisted without checking transcript membership and scoreCall still does not recheck rubric call_type.\\n**Why**: Full read-only validation of Codex review comments for the rubric scoring PR.\\n**Where**: src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric-scoring.service.ts; src/ai-rubric/schemas/ai-rubric-score.schema.ts; src/voice/voice-call/core/services/voice-call-transcript.service.ts\\n**Learned**: The existing Promise.allSettled checkpoint flow is a good fit for rejecting an invalid evidence quote: valid siblings are checkpointed and only the invalid criterion is retried.' --type discovery --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Found incomplete scoring-version coverage in rubric checkpoints\" $'**What**: Checkpoints fingerprint only criterion.updated_at even though the LLM input also includes rubric title/description, transcript/summary/language, model, and prompt policy; those inputs can change between BullMQ attempts and mix evaluation versions.\\n**Why**: Accurate and auditable scoring requires all criteria in a persisted score to use one coherent input/policy version.\\n**Where**: src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric-scoring.service.ts; src/ai-rubric/prompts/ai-rubric-score.prompt.ts; src/ai-rubric/consts/ai-rubric.consts.ts\\n**Learned**: The exact Codex criterion-edit finding is fixed, but the broader retry-version race remains.' --type discovery --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Found mutable rubric audit gap in persisted scores\" $'**What**: Score rows persist rubric/criterion IDs and outputs but no evaluated definition or scoring-policy version, while rubric updates preserve criterion IDs and can later edit or soft-delete their definitions.\\n**Why**: Historical scores may be silently reinterpreted under new definitions and cannot be reproduced or attributed to a prompt/model version.\\n**Where**: src/ai-rubric/models/ai-rubric-score.entity.ts; src/ai-rubric/models/ai-rubric-score-criteria.entity.ts; src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric.service.ts; src/ai-rubric/services/ai-rubric-criterion.service.ts\\n**Learned**: A definition snapshot or immutable rubric revision is required for a durable audit trail; retry fingerprints alone do not solve post-persistence edits.' --type discovery --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Confirmed PR 13405 goal is ticket_id per voice call\" $'**What**: User confirmed PR #13405 is the desired change to retain the ticket ID associated with each Vambe Phone/WhatsApp call.\\n**Why**: They need per-call ticket traceability so the pipeline can still be derived after the contact ticket closes.\\n**Where**: PR #13405; voice_call.ticket_id and its call-creation/backfill paths.\\n**Learned**: New calls capture the active ticket; AI calls may receive it during post-call backfill, while historical calls remain null unless separately backfilled.' --type preference --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Ignored Serena metadata in vambeai-backend\" $'**What**: Added `.serena/` to `.gitignore`.\\n**Why**: Repository instructions require local Serena indexing metadata to stay out of Git.\\n**Where**: /Users/sebabreguel/vambe/all_vambe/vambeai-backend/.gitignore' --type config --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Fixed ticket snapshot compatibility in PR 13405\" $'**What**: Hardened voice_call.ticket_id capture: Twilio and WhatsApp AI ticket reads use PostgreSQL primary, WhatsApp AI rows receive the known ticket at creation, and entry-stage calls without a ticket persist null instead of an invalid empty UUID; post-call backfill remains as fallback.\\n**Why**: Replica lag could miss a ticket created immediately before the call, AI rows unnecessarily waited until post-call, and the existing empty-string sentinel would fail against the new uuid foreign key.\\n**Where**: src/voice/voice-call/voice-call-api/services/voice-call-api.service.ts; src/whatsapp/whatsapp-call/core/services/whatsapp-call.service.ts; src/whatsapp/whatsapp-call/ai/call/whatsapp-ai-voice-call.service.ts; src/whatsapp/whatsapp-call/ai/session/whatsapp-ai-call-session.service.ts; related specs.\\n**Learned**: AiContactGetService.getAiContactById defaults to a replica unless useMaster is explicit. Outbound WhatsApp AI legitimately supports an entry-stage fallback with no active ticket, so the DB snapshot must stay nullable while the existing media-stream payload keeps its empty-string compatibility sentinel.' --type bugfix --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "gh pr edit 13405 --body \"## Context\\n\\nHoy no hay forma de saber de qué pipeline fue una llamada (vambe-phone / WhatsApp) una vez que el ticket del contacto se cierra: la única ruta era `voice_call → ai_contact → active_ticket_v2 → current_stage → pipeline`, y `active_ticket_v2` cambia o queda null cuando el ticket deja de estar activo.\\n\\n## What's new\\n\\n- Nueva columna `voice_call.ticket_id` (uuid nullable, FK a `ticket_v2`, index `idx_voice_call_ticket_id`): snapshot del ticket activo al crear la llamada. Como el ticket cerrado no se borra, el pipeline queda derivable: `voice_call.ticket_id → ticket_v2.current_stage → pipeline`.\\n- Twilio lee el contacto desde PostgreSQL primary para no perder un ticket recién creado por lag de réplica.\\n- WhatsApp humano guarda el ticket activo entregado por el contacto.\\n- WhatsApp AI guarda de inmediato el `ticketId` que ya resolvió para la sesión, tanto inbound como outbound. Si el flujo usa entry-stage y todavía no existe ticket, persiste `null` (nunca un UUID vacío).\\n- El post-call conserva un backfill idempotente (`UPDATE` solo cuando `ticket_id IS NULL`) para filas legacy o llamadas cuyo ticket aparezca después.\\n- Migración `1785532788472-add-voice-call-ticket-id.ts` limitada a columna, índice y FK. **Aún no corrida.**\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- 96 tests focalizados: OK.\\n- `pnpm typecheck`: OK.\\n- ESLint de archivos tocados: OK.\\n- Prettier de archivos tocados: OK.\\n\\n## Considerations\\n\\n- Llamadas históricas quedan con `ticket_id = null`; se puede hacer un backfill one-shot si se necesita.\\n- `ticket_id` es nullable porque existen llamadas válidas donde todavía no hay ticket.\\n- No se snapshotea `stage_id`: si el ticket se mueve de pipeline después, el join refleja el pipeline actual del ticket.\\n- Falta correr `pnpm migration:run` contra dev antes de mergear.\""], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Configured Serena for Mole\" $'**What**: Activated Serena for the repo, added .serena/ to .gitignore, and created durable project onboarding memories.\\n**Why**: Repository instructions require Serena on first interaction and local indexing metadata must stay out of Git.\\n**Where**: .gitignore and local .serena/ memories.\\n**Learned**: The code-review graph is empty and requires user approval before building.' --type config --project mole --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "/usr/bin/time -p env MOLE_TEST_NO_AUTH=1 MOLE_DRY_RUN=1 ./mole clean --dry-run > /dev/null"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Found mo clean performance hotspots\" $'**What**: Audited the mo clean orchestration and found repeated dry-run safety validation, double directory sizing for orphaned app data, sequential large-file size probes, and a bounded but high-multiplication project-artifact scan.\\n**Why**: The user requested a full complexity/performance optimization audit of mo clean.\\n**Where**: bin/clean.sh; lib/core/app_protection.sh; lib/clean/apps.sh; lib/clean/user.sh; lib/clean/hints.sh\\n**Learned**: _safe_clean_impl validates paths before record_dry_run_cleanup_target, which validates them again; normal protection can scan 478 bundle patterns and 349 data patterns per target. probe_project_artifact_hints can perform about 34 target checks for each of up to 200 projects and 120 nested dirs. An empty-HOME dry-run measured 27.33s, with 82 safe_clean path scans totaling 1.439s.' --type discovery --project Mole --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Found mo clean core performance hotspots\" $'**What**: Audited shared `mo clean` core without edits. Found repeated protected-path scans, duplicate dry-run sizing/ledger registration in `safe_find_delete` and `safe_sudo_find_delete`, and per-operation log setup that forks repeatedly. Local measurements: 200 `should_protect_path` misses took ~2.03s; 200 `append_log_line /dev/null` calls took ~3.29s versus direct append ~0s; 200 timestamps took ~0.44s.\\n**Why**: User requested a full complexity/performance optimization audit of `mo clean`.\\n**Where**: lib/core/app_protection.sh:514-548; lib/core/file_ops.sh:1550-1730; lib/core/log.sh:30-53; lib/core/base.sh:380-490; bin/clean.sh:929-958.\\n**Learned**: Protection arrays contain 481 path patterns plus a 352-pattern filename fallback; hot loops call a shell helper for each pattern. The graph index is empty and must not be built without user approval.' --type discovery --project Mole --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: mo clean complexity audit\" $'## Goal\\nAudit the mo clean execution path for algorithmic and performance complexity without editing files.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- Dry-run safe_clean paths are safety-validated in _safe_clean_impl and then validated again by record_dry_run_cleanup_target.\\n- should_protect_path may traverse 478 bundle patterns, and should_protect_data may traverse 349 data patterns per target.\\n- clean_orphaned_app_data sizes each orphan before safe_clean, which sizes it again.\\n- check_large_file_candidates runs independent du probes sequentially.\\n- probe_project_artifact_hints checks 34 target names across up to 200 projects and 120 nested dirs, about 822k possible directory tests before its wall-clock cap.\\n- Empty-HOME mo clean --dry-run measured 27.33s; 82 safe_clean path scans totaled 1.439s. Router dispatch uses exec and is not a hotspot.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Read the project bug catalog, ran the bundled complexity scanner, inspected routing/orchestration and key clean helpers, and gathered baseline timing. No files modified.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Implement the prevalidated dry-run ledger path first, then remove orphan double sizing; benchmark and test before considering larger parallelization/refactors.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- bin/clean.sh — command orchestration, safe_clean, dry-run ledger\\n- lib/core/app_protection.sh — protection and whitelist hot loops\\n- lib/clean/apps.sh — orphan scans and double sizing\\n- lib/clean/user.sh — sequential large-file probes\\n- lib/clean/hints.sh — project-artifact scan' --type session_summary --project Mole --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: Mole core clean complexity audit\" $'## Goal\\nAudit shared core used by `mo clean` for complexity and performance without editing.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- `should_protect_path` scans 481 full-path patterns plus a 352-pattern filename fallback; a miss costs ~10ms/path locally and is often invoked twice.\\n- `append_log_line` re-runs file preparation for every operation although log files are prepared at source time; 200 calls cost ~3.29s locally.\\n- `safe_find_delete` and `safe_sudo_find_delete` double-size and double-register dry-run targets.\\n- Repeated pattern-specific sudo finds can traverse the same tree multiple times.\\n- Code-review graph is empty and needs user approval before building.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Read Mole bug catalog and complexity optimizer references.\\n- Ran the bundled scanner; it does not analyze shell, so completed a manual symbol/call-site audit.\\n- Benchmarked protection matching, log append setup, timestamps, and validator components.\\n- Sent ranked findings, risks, and verification plan to the root agent. No files modified.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Root agent should prioritize single authoritative dry-run sizing/registration, cheap log append after one-time setup, and redundant protection-check removal while keeping final validation.\\n- Add focused Bats counters and before/after 1k-path benchmark if implementing.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- lib/core/app_protection.sh — protected-path matcher hot loop.\\n- lib/core/file_ops.sh — safe find/delete, validation, sizing, dry-run registration.\\n- lib/core/log.sh — append and operation logging.\\n- lib/core/base.sh — ensure_user_file/dir subprocess work.\\n- bin/clean.sh — preflight eligibility and sizing pipeline.\\n- tests/core_safe_functions.bats — deletion safety regressions.\\n- tests/clean_core.bats — clean preview/real parity.' --type session_summary --project Mole --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "gh pr diff 13429 > /tmp/pr13429.diff && printf '\\n-- diff summary --\\n' && git diff --stat dev...HEAD && printf '\\n-- reviews --\\n' && gh pr view 13429 --json reviews,comments --jq '{reviews:[.reviews[]|{author:.author.login,state,body}],comments:[.comments[]|{author:.author.login,body}]}'"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Found stale local dev ref during PR 13429 review\" $'**What**: Local `git diff dev...HEAD` produced an unrelated 1,021-file diff because the local `dev` ref is stale; PR review scope must use `gh pr diff 13429` or a refreshed base ref.\\n**Why**: Prevent reviewers from analyzing unrelated changes and issuing invalid findings.\\n**Where**: PR #13429 review in /Users/sebabreguel/vambe/voiceScoring/vambeai-backend.\\n**Learned**: The GitHub PR itself contains only eight changed files.' --type discovery --project vambeai-backend --scope project && engram save \"Created root handoff for PR 13429 review\" $'**What**: Created `handoff-pr-13429-review.md` at the repository root with the partial review state, decisions, open questions, tooling gotchas, and continuation steps.\\n**Why**: The user explicitly requested a handoff in the repository root.\\n**Where**: /Users/sebabreguel/vambe/voiceScoring/vambeai-backend/handoff-pr-13429-review.md.\\n**Learned**: No final verdict, tests, fixes, or GitHub review were completed before the handoff.' --type decision --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Session summary: handed off PR 13429 review\" $'## Goal\\nCreate a repository-root handoff for the interrupted review of PR #13429.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n- Keep the review read-only unless the user requests fixes or GitHub comments.\\n- Preserve the intentional best-effort, single-attempt, voice_human-only scoring design.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- Local `dev` is stale: `git diff dev...HEAD` shows 1,021 unrelated files, while GitHub reports eight PR files.\\n- The code-review graph was last updated 2026-07-23 and was not rebuilt.\\n- The checkout contains unrelated untracked `.context/`, `.serena/`, `data/`, and `plan-runs/` paths.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Inspected PR metadata and production diff.\\n- Created and verified the root handoff with current state, open review questions, and continuation guidance.\\n- No code changes, tests, GitHub comments, or final verdict were produced.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Resume from the handoff, finish the focused review, run targeted tests/typecheck, and report actionable findings.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- handoff-pr-13429-review.md — authoritative handoff for continuing the review.\\n- /tmp/pr13429.diff — temporary machine-local GitHub PR diff, if still present.' --type session_summary --project vambeai-backend --scope project"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["git", "fetch", "origin", "pull/15605/head"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["git", "fetch", "origin", "c000c2dc0b884015cc16a053b1aa2e1b0ab75d4e"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["node", "-e", "const p=require(\"child_process\").spawn(\"engram\",[\"mcp\",\"--tools=mem_session_summary\"],{stdio:[\"pipe\",\"pipe\",\"pipe\"]});let b=\"\";p.stdout.on(\"data\",x=>{b+=x;for(let i;(i=b.indexOf(\"\\n\"))>=0;){const l=b.slice(0,i);b=b.slice(i+1);try{const r=JSON.parse(l);if(r.id===1){p.stdin.write(JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:\"2.0\",method:\"notifications/initialized\"})+\"\\n\");p.stdin.write(JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:\"2.0\",id:2,method:\"tools/list\",params:{}})+\"\\n\")}if(r.id===2){console.log(JSON.stringify(r));p.kill()}}catch{}}});p.stdin.write(JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:\"2.0\",id:1,method:\"initialize\",params:{protocolVersion:\"2024-11-05\",capabilities:{},clientInfo:{name:\"codex\",version:\"1\"}}})+\"\\n\");setTimeout(()=>p.kill(),10000);"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["node", "-e", "const p=require(\"child_process\").spawn(\"engram\",[\"mcp\",\"--tools=mem_session_summary\",\"--project\",\"vambeai-backend\"],{stdio:[\"pipe\",\"pipe\",\"pipe\"]});let b=\"\";const t=setTimeout(()=>p.kill(),10000);p.stdout.on(\"data\",x=>{b+=x;for(let i;(i=b.indexOf(\"\\n\"))>=0;){const l=b.slice(0,i);b=b.slice(i+1);try{const r=JSON.parse(l);if(r.id===1){p.stdin.write(JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:\"2.0\",method:\"notifications/initialized\"})+\"\\n\");p.stdin.write(JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:\"2.0\",id:2,method:\"tools/call\",params:{name:\"mem_session_summary\",arguments:{content:\"## Goal\\nReview GitHub PR vambeai/vambeai-backend#15605 without modifying code or publishing comments.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- Confirmed P2: both legacy draft consumers omit custom backoffStrategy although existing jobs retain backoff.type=custom. If forwarding fails, BullMQ throws Unknown backoff strategy custom before moving job to retry/failed, leaving stalled recovery.\\n- Restoring customBackoff without alwaysRetry:true will not retry plain dispatcher errors; alternatively wrap as retryable BullError.\\n- No other actionable introduced bugs confirmed by producer, wiring and final reviewers.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Reviewed isolated /tmp/vambe-pr15605-review at fa35ff8138295ade968dd6bd34ab1f6722511d5c against merge-base 5debce9aa94adb04bf5abd187e503175404c61d3.\\n- 16 targeted suites passed, 357 tests (14 changed suites plus 2 send-consumer suites).\\n- Targeted ESLint passed on 4 files; git diff --check passed. Full suite/typecheck not run.\\n- Main and isolated tracked worktrees unchanged; no GitHub comments posted. Engram discovery #2 saved.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Report one P2 finding; fix both legacy worker retry strategies and add regression tests if requested.\\n- Isolated review worktree remains at /tmp/vambe-pr15605-review.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- src/ai/construct-ai-run-module/core/consumers/legacy-draft-construct-ai-run.consumer.ts:8 — missing custom backoff worker strategy.\\n- src/ai/ai-run-module/core/consumers/legacy-draft-ai-run.consumer.ts:8 — same defect.\\n\",project:\"vambeai-backend\"}}})+\"\\n\")}if(r.id===2){console.log(JSON.stringify(r));clearTimeout(t);p.kill()}}catch{}}});p.stdin.write(JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:\"2.0\",id:1,method:\"initialize\",params:{protocolVersion:\"2024-11-05\",capabilities:{},clientInfo:{name:\"codex\",version:\"1\"}}})+\"\\n\");"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["node", "-e", "const p=require(\"child_process\").spawn(\"engram\",[\"mcp\",\"--tools=mem_session_summary\",\"--project\",\"vambeai-backend\"],{stdio:[\"pipe\",\"pipe\",\"pipe\"]});let b=\"\";const t=setTimeout(()=>p.kill(),10000);p.stdout.on(\"data\",x=>{b+=x;for(let i;(i=b.indexOf(\"\\n\"))>=0;){const l=b.slice(0,i);b=b.slice(i+1);try{const r=JSON.parse(l);if(r.id===1){p.stdin.write(JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:\"2.0\",method:\"notifications/initialized\"})+\"\\n\");p.stdin.write(JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:\"2.0\",id:2,method:\"tools/call\",params:{name:\"mem_session_summary\",arguments:{content:\"## Goal\\nExpand PR 15605 review using user-requested .claude/agents/pr-reviewer.md categories rather than confirmed bugs only.\\n\\n## Discoveries\\n- Prior P2 legacy custom-backoff defect remains the production-risk finding.\\n- IMPORTANT: lane-dispatcher-wiring-guard.spec.ts:93 accepts a module name anywhere, including TS import. Executed actual unchanged guard with mocked file read removing AiRunDispatcherModule only from Nest imports; original and broken variant both pass.\\n- IMPORTANT: new dispatcher routing/options/client grouping and background/legacy failure behavior lack direct behavioral tests; source-pattern guards and mocked producer tests do not cover these.\\n- Fixed per-client group caps only represent 25 percent at eight replicas/default concurrency; document operational assumption, not current production bug.\\n\\n## Accomplished\\n- Read requested reviewer instructions and independently revalidated important suggestions with tech-lead reviewer.\\n- Ran full guard in memory with mutation, without file edits.\\n- Prior verification remains 16 suites/357 tests passing and focused lint passing; no new code changes.\\n- Saved user review-framework preference #6 and guard discovery #7.\\n\\n## Next Steps\\n- Report critical existing retry issue, two important test suggestions, and conditional capacity consideration. No minor nitpicks.\\n\\n## Relevant Files\\n- .claude/agents/pr-reviewer.md — requested review categories.\\n- src/ai/common/run-lane/lane-dispatcher-wiring-guard.spec.ts:93 — guard false negative.\\n- src/ai/ai-run-module/core/dispatcher/ai-run-dispatcher.service.ts:28 — representative untested dispatcher logic.\\n- src/ai/ai-run-module/core/consumers/background-ai-run.consumer.ts:8 — fixed group cap.\\n\",project:\"vambeai-backend\"}}})+\"\\n\")}if(r.id===2){console.log(JSON.stringify(r));clearTimeout(t);p.kill()}}catch{}}});p.stdin.write(JSON.stringify({jsonrpc:\"2.0\",id:1,method:\"initialize\",params:{protocolVersion:\"2024-11-05\",capabilities:{},clientInfo:{name:\"codex\",version:\"1\"}}})+\"\\n\");"], decision="allow")
prefix_rule(pattern=["/bin/zsh", "-lc", "engram save \"Review PR 15799 at ed1e0cf\" $'## Goal\\nReview live GitHub PR15799 and current implementation ed1e0cf3fb0344b364061ba1b10d6c9b8e4b5479, focusing delta since a8413f5ef0.\\n## Discoveries\\nPR now explicitly accepts late summaries and defers stronger judge evaluation; duration30-59s formatting fixed. New replica query has proper finally release, ticket/client scoping, duration>=30 and ASC take10. Cap occurs before summary filtering so voicemail/empty summaries consume slots; documented raw-call policy, not confirmed bug. Raw webhook direction claim is not proven DB provenance: inspected receiveStatus uses Direction for logs/websocket, not persistence; avoid claiming confirmed mislabeled production calls. Security report CI failure is artifact finalize403, not a reported code vulnerability.\\n## Accomplished\\n100 targeted tests across5 suites pass, typecheck/diff-check pass. GitHub lint/static/dependency/knip/SAST pass; test1 still running at last check. No new blocking code defect confirmed. No source edits or GitHub comments. HEAD matches PR and working tree clean.\\n## Next Steps\\nWait remaining CI; retry/fix security artifact upload permissions. Optional improve usable-summary cap and expand judge evaluation per documented follow-up.\\n## Relevant Files\\nsrc/voice/voice-call/core/services/voice-call-transcript.service.ts — replica query duration/cap.\\nsrc/ai-rubric/modules/rubric-strategy/ticket/scorable-ticket.service.ts — summary mapping/filter.\\nsrc/ai-rubric/utils/ticket-transcript.ts — fixed duration threshold.\\nhttps://github.com/vambeai/vambeai-backend/pull/15799 — reviewed body/checks.' --type session_summary --project vambeai-backend"], decision="allow")
